                                                "text": "Cpl. Perez, the radio sup said, \"Everything checks out OK, Sarge. We're up and working.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "708fad5f-1829-4b92-85fe-d494455dd1e1",
                                                "sense_id": "f8a18f87-339b-3e40-a385-ce5fe574680f",
                                                "text": "But here comes the deputy vehicle, cruising right up to the shelter on the bike path. The sup is a retired county sheriff's deputy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "sup",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3c8b36f2-efa1-3d96-aac8-a516fcd253fa",
                                        "entry_id": "945d7224-0c3f-3cb0-975c-bc9eefbb2e74",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To eat supper."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "162b682f-aef8-44fe-8354-f075849b3b09",
                                                "sense_id": "3c8b36f2-efa1-3d96-aac8-a516fcd253fa",
                                                "text": "...I propose we should have up the cold pie, and let him sup."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "15dfb189-3954-4f34-b833-4f78728d968d",
                                                "sense_id": "3c8b36f2-efa1-3d96-aac8-a516fcd253fa",
                                                "text": "I pray you, be seated and sup how you please. You will, I trust, excuse me that I do not join you; but I have dined already, and I do not sup."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "sup",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5ba5da5a-316e-3d2f-8bfe-a4d14452ca67",
                                        "entry_id": "bca7d77f-92b5-32ca-8850-f3e4f4e5599b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To sip; to take a small amount of food or drink into the mouth, especially with a spoon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb0d1995-71fc-4055-b635-8509be338395",
                                                "sense_id": "5ba5da5a-316e-3d2f-8bfe-a4d14452ca67",
                                                "text": "There I'll sup / Balm and nectar in my cup."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33faaaef-0a54-4400-8522-97b41cfa5337",
                                                "sense_id": "5ba5da5a-316e-3d2f-8bfe-a4d14452ca67",
                                                "text": "We stood upon the forehead of the hills, / And lifted up our hearts in prayer; / And as we halted, reverent, / Meseemed that Nature o’er us bent, / That she did bid us sup / From bread she gave and from her cup."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "961bb970-62a7-4709-8ec1-216a95bfa8fc",
                                                "sense_id": "5ba5da5a-316e-3d2f-8bfe-a4d14452ca67",
                                                "text": "On market days the farmers would come in before going home - Tysons and Lindsays and Birketts and Longmires and Boows and Dawsons - and their dogs would lie in heaps on the flags while they themselves supped Gerald's ale."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "sup",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3fe5c687-41a0-35a2-b72e-226dab0a3150",
                                        "entry_id": "90ec5521-f27e-32be-90b5-6961879993e1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sip; a small amount, of food or drink, water or rain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d95dd77c-916f-4480-b173-f26a8ff7817b",
                                                "sense_id": "3fe5c687-41a0-35a2-b72e-226dab0a3150",
                                                "text": "Is it stoppin' there you'd be till every sup of the say's dhrained out on us to beyant the King Pharaoh's Islands?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "df75159e-0c54-4012-b363-88c138b602cd",
                                                "sense_id": "3fe5c687-41a0-35a2-b72e-226dab0a3150",
                                                "text": "“Then, who,” the sick man meekly said, / “Shall heal the sick and hide the dead?— / “Snatch the despairer’s poisoned cup; / Clothe shame, and give the outcast sup?⁠— / “Lighten, if only by a hair, / The load of human pain and care?”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "54e11fe4-680d-45d4-887e-4504c3ab9953",
                                                "sense_id": "3fe5c687-41a0-35a2-b72e-226dab0a3150",
                                                "text": "We’re sisters in a sort and I’ll take Louie home with me and give her sup and shelter."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "56187cea-0a04-4ea5-8a18-8e4c126a0ffa",
                                                "sense_id": "3fe5c687-41a0-35a2-b72e-226dab0a3150",
                                                "text": "... an' we'll bathe them eyes of yours with a sup of rain water, the way when you go indoors ne'er a one will see there's been a ha'porth the matter."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b2e812a-cf78-4762-8e46-3d1e4ace7d86",
                                                "sense_id": "3fe5c687-41a0-35a2-b72e-226dab0a3150",
                                                "text": "A long, long sup of beer flowed gratefully down his gullet."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c499824d-6009-4bd1-a442-ff759f7d3a77",
                                                "sense_id": "3fe5c687-41a0-35a2-b72e-226dab0a3150",
                                                "text": "The hands touch B upon the head, give him sup from a cup and wipe his brow with a cloth, and finally embrace him as he slumps back down upon his desk."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55777828-de7f-42e7-a15f-0143049585de",
                                                "sense_id": "3fe5c687-41a0-35a2-b72e-226dab0a3150",
                                                "text": "'Wouldn't the fields be glad of a sup of rain.' 'Won't we have the rain for long enough.'"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "sup",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dd736888-b73a-3fde-a6cf-02d8421a7c65",
                                        "entry_id": "8ecd8e40-8306-35ed-bdda-b4ce3076dd57",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "what's up (either as a greeting or actual question)"
                                        ],
